hadiths[135]{hadithnumber,text}:
"608","Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \When one of you makes a supplication"
"609","Abu Nu'aym, who is Wahb, said, \I saw Ibn 'Umar and Ibn az-Zubayr\nmaking supplication"
"610","'A'isha say that she saw the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, making supplication with his hands raised, saying, 'I am a man,\nso do not punish me. If I harm any man of the believers or revile him,\ndo not punish me for that.'\""611"""
"611","Ali narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: ""Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused; so invoke Allah against them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced the qiblah and raised his hands. The people thought he was invoking against them. He said: 'O Allah, guide Daws and bring them.'"""
"612","Anas said, \No rain fell for a year and so one of the Muslims went\nto the Prophet"
"613","'Ikrima heard 'A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, say that\nshe saw the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, raise his\nhands in supplication, saying, 'O Allah, I am only a man, so do not punish\nme. If I harm or revile a Muslim man, do not punish me for it!'\""614"""
"614","Arim narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that Al-Tufayl ibn Amr said to the Prophet ﷺ: ""Would you like a fortress and protection, the fortress of Daws?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ declined, because of what Allah had destined for the Ansar. So Al-Tufayl emigrated, and a man from his people emigrated with him. The man fell ill, so he became distressed — or a word similar to it — and he dragged himself to a horn (a projecting rock), took a sharp knife, cut his jugular veins, and died. Al-Tufayl saw him in a dream and said: 'What was done with you?' He said: 'I was forgiven because of my emigration to the Prophet ﷺ.' He said: 'What is the matter with your hands?' He said: 'It was said: We do not repair for you what you corrupted of your hands.' Al-Tufayl related this to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'O Allah, and for his hands, forgive,' and he raised his hands."""
"615","Anas ibn Malik said, \The Messenger of Allah"
"616","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said that Allah Almighty said, \I am according\nto My slave's opinion of Me"
"617","Shaddad ibn Aws reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \The best way of asking forgiveness is 'O Allah"
"618","Ibn 'Umar said, \We used to say this a hundred times in the assembly\nof the Prophet"
"619","'A'isha said, \The Messenger of Allah"
"620","Abu Mu'ammar narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, saying: Husayn narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, saying: Bushayr ibn Ka'b al-Adawi narrated to me, saying: Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to me, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""The chief of seeking forgiveness (Sayyid al-Istighfar) is to say: 'O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no deity but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You.' Whoever says it during the day with certainty in it, and dies that day before evening, he is from the people of Paradise. And whoever says it at night while certain of it, and dies before morning, he is from the people of Paradise."""
"621","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar said, \I heard the Prophet"
"622","'Glory be to Allah';\n'Praise be to Allah'; and 'There is no god but Allah' a hundred times.\""623"""
"623","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us. Abdullah ibn Yazid said to me: ""I heard Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'The swiftest supplication to be answered is the supplication of an absent person for an absent person.'"""
"624","Abu Bakr as-Siddiq was heard to say, \The supplication of a brother\nin Allah is answered.\"""""
"625","Safwan ibn 'Abdullah ibn Safwan, who was married to the daughter\nof Abu'd-Darda', said, \I visited them in Syria and found Umm ad-Darda'\nin the house"
"626","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr reported that a man said, \O Allah"
"627","Ibn 'Umar said, \I heard the Prophet"
"628","Ibn 'Umar said, \I make supplication in everything I do - even\nthat Allah will make the stride of my animal long so that I find ease in\nthat.\"""""
"629","It is reported that 'Umar used to make supplication with his words,\n\) Allah"
"630","'Our Lord, make peace between us and guide us on the path of Islam.\nSave us from the darkness (and bring us) to the light. Remove acts of deviance\nfrom us, both open and hidden. Bless us in our ears, our eyes, our hearts,\nour wives and our children. Turn to us. You are the Ever-Turning back (to his slaves), Most\nMerciful. Make us thankful for Your blessing and make us among those who\ngive praise for it and proclaim it. Perfect it for us.\""631"""
"631","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: ""When Anas supplicated for his brother, he would say: 'May Allah cause a people of righteousness, who are neither wrongdoers nor sinners, to pray upon him; they stand the night in prayer and fast the day.'"""
"632","'Amr ibn al-Harith said, \My mother took me to the Prophet"
"633","Anas ibn Malik was told, \Your brothers have come to you from Basra\n(and that day he was at the zawiyya) wanting for you to make supplication\nto Allah for them.\"" He said"
"634","The Prophet took a reed, split it, and then did not split it. Then he split it, and then did not split it. Then he split it and it split. He said, ""Indeed, God is pure, and praise is due to God, and there is no god but God. He erases sins just as a tree sheds its leaves."""
"635","Anas reported that a woman came to the Prophet, to complain to\nhim of a need. He said, 'Shall I show you something better than that? You\nshould say, 'There is no god but Allah' 33 times when you go to sleep and\nsay 'Glory be to Allah' 33 times and say 'Praise be to Allah' 34 times\nand then that hundred is better than his world and all that it contains.'\""636"""
"636","And the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Whoever says 'La ilaha illa Allah' one hundred times, 'Subhan Allah' one hundred times, and 'Allahu Akbar' one hundred times, it is better for him than freeing ten slaves and sacrificing seven camels."""
"637","A man came to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace,\nand said, \Messenger of Allah"
"638","'Glory be to Allah\nwho has no partner. His is the Kingdom and praise is His and He has power\nover all things. There is no power nor strength except by Allah. Glory be\nto Allah and by His praise.\""639"""
"639","Al-Salt ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Jabr ibn Habib, from Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: ""The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was praying, and he had a need, so I delayed for him. He said: 'O Aisha, adhere to the concise and comprehensive supplications.' When I finished, I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what are the concise and comprehensive supplications?' He said: 'Say: O Allah, I ask You for all good, its immediate and its deferred, what I know of it and what I do not know. And I seek refuge in You from all evil, its immediate and its deferred, what I know of it and what I do not know. And I ask You for Paradise and what brings one closer to it of word or deed. And I seek refuge in You from the Fire and what brings one closer to it of word or deed. And I ask You for what Muhammad ﷺ asked You, and I seek refuge in You from what Muhammad ﷺ sought refuge from. And whatever You have decreed for me, make its outcome guidance.'"""
"640","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \If any Muslim does not have anything to\ngive as sadaqa"
"641","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \If anyone says"
"642","Here is the translated text in English:Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Salmah b. Wirdan narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas and Malik b. Aus b. al-Hadathan, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) went out to relieve himself, but did not find anyone to follow him. Then Umar went out and followed him with a cloak or a turban, and found him in a valley, so he waited until the Prophet (peace be upon him) raised his head and said: ""You have done well, O Umar, when you found me in this valley and waited for me, for indeed Gabriel came to me and said: 'Whoever greets you with a single greeting, Allah will greet him tenfold, and will raise him ten degrees.'"""
"643","Anas ibn Malik reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \If anyone says the prayer on me once"
"644","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, went up the minbar. When he reached the first\nstep, he said, \Amen\"". When he ascended to the second step"
"645","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \If anyone prays once on me"
"646","that the Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: “Amin, Amin, Amin.” He was asked: O Messenger of Allah, you did not used to do this? He said:“Jibril said to me: ‘May the nose of a servant be rubbed in the dust who ˹lives to see˺ his parents, or one of them, yet they do not cause him to enter Jannah.’ So I said: ‘Amin.’ Then he said: ‘May the nose of a servant be rubbed in the dust who has Ramadan come upon him and is not forgiven.’ So I said: ‘Amin.’ Then he said: ‘May the nose of a man be rubbed in the dust in whose presence you are mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you.’ So I said: ‘Amin.’”"
"647","'Glory be to Allah and by His praise in number as great as His creation\nand in accordance with His own pleasure and the weight of His Throne and\nthe extent of His words.'\""648"""
"648","Ibn Salam narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from Hellfire. Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave. Seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the False Messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal). Seek refuge with Allah from the trials of life and death."""
"649","Jabir reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \O Allah"
"650","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, used to say, \O Allah"
"651","Tariq ibn Ashyam al-Ashja'i said, \We used to go and visit the\nProphet"
"652","Umm Qays reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said to her, \What she said will make her life long. They said"
"653","The Prophet would enter upon us, the family of the house. One day, he entered and said, ""O Allah, increase his wealth and children, prolong his life, and forgive him."""
"654","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \The supplication of any of you is answered\nas long as he does not get impatient and say"
"655","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \The supplication of any of you is answered\nas long as he does not make supplication for something which is a wrong\naction or cutting off ties of kinship or become impatient and say"
"656","'Amr ibn Shu'ayb reported that his grandfather said, \I heard the\nProphet"
"657","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, used to seek refuge with Allah from the evils of life\nand death and the punishment of the grave and the evil of the Dajjal.\""658"""
"658","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Malih Subayh narrated to us, saying: Abu Salih narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""Whoever does not ask Allah, Allah becomes angry with him."""
"659","Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \When you call on Allah"
"660","'Uthman said that he heard the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, say, \A person will not be harmed by anything if he says\nevery morning and evening 33 times"
"661","when the call to prayer has been given\nand when in battle ranks in the Cause of Allah.\""662"""
"662","Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, from Lu'lu'ah, from Abu Sirma, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: 'O Allah, I ask You for my independence (ghina) and the independence of my master (mawla).'"""
"663","'O Allah, protect me from the evil\nof my sight and hearing, my tongue, my heart, and the evil of my desire.'\""664"""
"664","Qabisah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Taliq ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, who said: ""The Prophet ﷺ used to say: 'O Allah, help me and do not help against me, grant me victory and do not grant victory against me, and make guidance easy for me.'"""
"665","'O Allah, help me\nand do not help anyone against me. Devise for me and do not devise against\nme. Make guidance easy for me. Avert from me the one who attacks me. O\nLord, make me grateful to You, remember You, fearful of You, obedient to\nYou and humble to You, supplicating, penitent. Accept my repentance. Wash\naway my wrong actions and answer my supplication. Establish my proof and\nguide my heart. Make my tongue correct and make resentment flow out of\nmy heart.'\""666"""
"666","Isma'il narrated to us, saying: Malik narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Ziyad, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, who said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said on the pulpit: ""Indeed, there is no preventer for what You have given, and no giver for what Allah has withheld, and the fortune of a fortunate person does not avail him. And whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding of the religion. I heard these words from the Prophet ﷺ on these wooden sticks (i.e., the pulpit)."""
"667","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \The firmest supplication is to say"
"668","'O Allah, make my deen\ncorrect - it is the support of my affairs. Make my deen correct -\nit contains my livelihood. Make death a mercy for me from every evil.'\""669"""
"669","Ali narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sumayy narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: ""The Prophet ﷺ used to seek refuge from the severity of affliction, the attainment of wretchedness, the evil of decree, and the rejoicing of enemies."""
"670","laziness, miserliness, bad pride,\nthe trial of what is in the breast, and the punishment of the grave.\""671"""
"671","Musaddad narrated to us, saying: Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father say: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: ""The Prophet ﷺ used to say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity and laziness, cowardice and old age. And I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death. And I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave.'"""
"672","Here is the translated text in English:He told us that 'Abdullah bin Sa'id bin Abi Hind told us, from 'Amr bin Abi 'Amr, from Anas, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge with You from worry, grief, inability, laziness, arrogance, miserliness, and being burdened with debt, and from being overcome by men."""
"673","Abu Hurayra said, \One of the supplications of the Prophet"
"674","He told us Amr ibn Marzooq, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to say: ""O Allah, I ask of You guidance, and purity, and sufficiency. And our companions, from Omar and Tuba."""
"675","Thumana ibn Huzn said, \I heard a shaykh call out in a loud voice"
"676","'Abdullah ibn Abi 'Awfa reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, used to say, \O Allah"
"677","Anas reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him\npeace, used to make supplication with this supplication, \O Allah"
"678","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, used to say, \O Allah"
"679","We were with the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he called for a great du'a that we did not memorize. We said, ""You called for a du'a that we did not memorize?"" He said, ""I will inform you of something that will gather all of that for you: O Allah, indeed we ask of You what Your Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, asked of You, and we seek refuge with You from what Your Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, sought refuge from, O Allah, You are the One who is sought for help and upon You is the responsibility, and there is no power or strength except with Allah, or as He said."""
"680","'Amr ibn Shu'ayb reported from his father that his grandfather said, \I heard the\nProphet"
"681","Ibn 'Abbas used to say, \O Allah"
"682","Anas said, \The most frequent supplication of the Prophet"
"683","The Prophet would often say: ""O Allah, You who changes hearts, fix my heart upon Your religion."""
"684","'O Allah, praise\nis Yours in quantity as great as the heavens and in quantity as great as\nthe earth and in quantity as great as You wish from anything else. O Allah,\npurify me with ice, snow and cold water. O Allah, purify me from wrong\nactions and clean me as the white garment is cleansed of dirt.'\""685"""
"685","Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abdullah ibn Dinan, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: ""It was from the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the loss of Your blessing, the change of Your well-being, the suddenness of Your vengeance, and all of Your wrath.'"""
"686","Our messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would leave his work, if he saw a young one in the upper part of the sky, and if he was in prayer, he would then turn towards him. If Allah revealed him, he would praise Allah, and if it rained, he would say: ""O Allah, send a beneficial rain."""
"687","Isma'il ibn Qays said, \I came to Khabbab when he had been cauterised\nseven times. He said"
"688","Abu Musa reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, used to make this supplication, \O Allah"
"689","Abu Musa al-Ash'ari used to use this supplication, \O Allah"
"690","Here is the translated text in English:Hadith:Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Haywa, who said: 'Uqba b. Muslim narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from as-Sunnabi, from Mu'adh b. Jabal, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) took my hand and said: ""O Mu'adh, I said: 'At your service.' He said: 'I love you.' I said: 'And I, by Allah, love you.' He said: 'Shall I teach you words to say at the end of every prayer?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Say: ""O Allah, assist me in remembering You, and in showing gratitude to You, and in the beauty of my worship to You.""'"""
"691","Here is the translated text in English:Hadith:It was narrated that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Praise be to Allah, a great deal, a pure, and a blessed praise, in which He is praised. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the companion of this statement? The man was silent, and he saw that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was displeased with something, so he said: Who is it? The man did not say anything except to nod, so a man said: I am, I hope for good with it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I saw thirteen angels descending, each of them trying to raise it to Allah, the Exalted, the Glorious."
"692","He narrated to us Abu al-Nu'man, who said: He narrated to us Sa'id bin Zayd, who said: He narrated to us 'Abd al-'Aziz bin Suhaib, who said: He narrated to me Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) would say when he intended to enter the lavatory: ""O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the evil and the stench."""
"693","'A'isha said, \When the Messenger of Allah"
"694","'I seek refuge with You from the punishment of Hellfire, and\nI seek refuge with You from the punishment of the grave. I seek refuge\nwith You from the trial of the Dajjal and the I seek refuge from the trials\nof life and death. I seek refuge with You from the trial of the grave.'\""695"""
"695","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, who said: ""I spent the night with Maymunah. The Prophet ﷺ got up, attended to his need, washed his face and hands, then slept. Then he got up, went to the water skin, untied its cord, then performed ablution — an ablution between two ablutions, not excessive but sufficient — and prayed. I stood up and stretched, disliking that he would see I had been awake. I performed ablution, then he stood to pray, and I stood at his left. He took my ear and turned me to his right. His prayer during the night totaled thirteen rak'ahs. Then he lay down and slept until he snored — and when he slept, he would snore. Bilal called him to prayer, and he prayed without performing ablution. And in his supplication was: 'O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my hearing, light on my right, light on my left, light above me, light below me, light in front of me, light behind me, and make light great for me.'"""
"696","The Prophet (peace be upon him) would stand up at night, perform his prayer, and then praise Allah for what He had blessed him with. Then, he would conclude his prayer with: ""O Allah, grant me light in my heart, and grant me light in my hearing, and grant me light in my sight, and grant me light from my right, and grant me light from my left, and grant me light from before me, and grant me light from behind me, and increase me in light, and increase me in light, and increase me in light."""
"697","When the Messenger of Allah would stand for prayer in the middle of the night, he would say: ""O Allah, praise is for You, You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them. Praise is for You, You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth. Praise is for You, You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them. You are the Truth, Your promise is the Truth, Your meeting is the Truth. Paradise is the Truth, Hell is the Truth, the Hour is the Truth. O Allah, I have submitted to You, I have believed in You, I have relied on You, I have turned to You, I have been defeated by You, I have been judged by You. Forgive me for what I have done in the past, and for what I have delayed, and for what I have hastened, and for what I have concealed, and for what I have revealed. You are my God, there is no god but You."""
"698","'O Allah, I ask You for pardon and good health in this world and the Next. O Allah, I ask You for good health\nin my deen and my family. Veil my faults and assuage my terror. Guard me before me, behind me, on my right and my left and above me. I seek refuge with You from unexpected destruction from beneath me.'\""699"""
"699","Ali narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Rifaa'ah al-Zuraqi narrated to us, from his father, who said: When it was the day of Uhud and the polytheists turned back, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Stand in rows so that I may praise my Lord, Mighty and Majestic."" So they stood behind him in rows. Then he said: ""O Allah, to You belongs all praise. O Allah, there is none who can withhold what You have granted, none who can bring near what You have put far, none who can put far what You have brought near, none who can give what You have withheld, and none who can withhold what You have given. O Allah, spread upon us from Your blessings, mercy, grace, and provision. O Allah, I ask You for the abiding bliss that neither changes nor ceases. O Allah, I ask You for bliss on the day of destitution, and security on the day of fear. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You have given us, and from the evil of what You have withheld from us. O Allah, make faith beloved to us and adorn it in our hearts, and make disbelief, wickedness, and disobedience hateful to us, and make us among the rightly guided. O Allah, cause us to die as Muslims, live us as Muslims, and join us with the righteous, not disgraced nor tested. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who bar from Your path and belie Your messengers, and place upon them Your wrath and punishment. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who were given the Scripture, O God of Truth."""
"700","'There is no\ngod but Allah, the Immense, the Forbearing. There is no god but Prophet,\nthe Lord of the heavens and the earth and the Lord of the Immense Throne.'\""701"""
"701","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Jalil narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Maymun, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to me, that he said to his father: ""O my father, I hear you supplicating every morning: 'O Allah, grant me well-being in my body. O Allah, grant me well-being in my hearing. O Allah, grant me well-being in my sight. There is no god but You,' repeating it three times when you enter the evening, and three times when you enter the morning. And you say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave. There is no god but You,' repeating it three times when you enter the evening, and three times when you enter the morning."" He said: ""Yes, my son. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying them, and I love to follow his Sunnah."""
"702","'There is no\ngod but Allah, the Immense, the Forbearing. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the Immense Throne, there is no god but Allah, the Lord of the heavens and the earth and the Lord of the Immense Throne.' O Allah, avert its evil.\""703"""
"703","Al-Mutarrif ibn Abdullah Abu al-Mus'ab narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the Istikharah (seeking guidance) in all matters just as he would teach us a Surah from the Qur'an. He said: ""When one of you is concerned about a matter, let him pray two rak'ahs, then say: 'O Allah, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek ability by Your power, and I ask You of Your great bounty. For You have power and I have none; You know and I know not; You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if You know that this matter is good for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair — or he said: in the immediate and the deferred of my affair — then decree it for me. And if You know that this matter is bad for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair — or he said: in the immediate and the deferred of my affair — then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, and decree for me the good wherever it may be, then make me content with it.' And he should name his need."""
"704","Here is the translated text in English:Ibrahim bin al-Munzir narrated to us, saying: Sufyan bin Hamzah narrated to us, saying: Kithir bin Zayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman bin Ka'b, saying: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) called out in this mosque, the mosque of the conquest, on the 2nd, 3rd, and 4th days, and he was responded to between the two prayers on the 4th day. Jabir said: And I did not experience a more significant and more intense matter, except that I would hasten to that time. So I called out to Allah between the two prayers on the 4th day at that time, except that I knew the response."
"705","He told us Ali bin Khalaf bin Khalifa, who said: He told me Hafiz bin Akhi Anas, who said: I was with the Prophet, peace be upon him, when a man called out: O Abdeessamawati, O Hayyu, O Qayyumu, I ask you. He said: Do you know what he called out? By the One Who is in His Hand, he called out Allah with the name that if He is called out with it, He responds."
"706","Abdullah bin Amr said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""Teach me a supplication that I can recite in my prayer."" He said: ""Say: O Allah, I have wronged myself greatly, and none but You forgives sins. So forgive me from Your mercy, for You are the Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful."""
"707","'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said, \When there is a ruler in charge of\nyou whose arrogance or injustice is feared"
"708","Ibn 'Abbas said, \When you go to an awesome ruler and fear that\nhe will attack you"
"709","Whoever is afflicted with worry or grief or hardship or fear of a ruler, and then calls out to these [things], they will be responded to. I ask of You, without any god but You, Lord of the seven heavens, and Lord of the great throne, and I ask of You, without any god but You, Lord of the seven heavens, and Lord of the generous throne, and I ask of You, without any god but You, Lord of the seven heavens, and Lord of the seven earths, and what is in them, for You are capable of all things. Then seek Allah's need."
"710","either his supplication is answered quickly, or it\nis stored up for him in the Next World, or an evil equal to it is averted\nfrom him.\ It was said"
"711","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \No believer turns his face to Allah and asks Him\nfor something but that He gives it to him"
"712","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \Nothing is dearer to Allah than supplication.\"""""
"713","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \The noblest act of worship is supplication.\"""""
"714","An-Nu'man ibn Bashir reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \Supplication is worship.' Then he recited"
"715","'A'isha said, \The Prophet"
"716","Maqil bin Yasar (ra) said that he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with Abu Bakr (ra). He said, \O Abu Bakr"
"717","The Prophet (peace be upon him) would say: ""O Allah, I ask of You good for what has been sent with it, and I seek refuge with You from the evil that has been sent with it."""
"718","\ O Allah cause this wind to bring rain and let it not be without benefit\""."""
"719","(O Allah! We ask you the good of this wind and the good of what is therein and the good with which it is sent.)"
"720","It is stated by sayidina Abu Hurayrah (ra) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said \Wind is the mercy of Allah. It brings mercy or punishment. Do not denounce it but ask Allah"
"721","It is reported by Salim bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Abdullah bin Umar (ra)) that when the prophet (ﷺ) heard a thunder-clap or a thunder-bolt, he would make this supplication:“O Allah, slay us not with your lightening and destroy us not with your punishment. But, preserve us before that.”"
"722","“Glory be to him whom you glorified.” He said that the thunderclap is an angel who yells at the rainclouds as a shepherd yells at his sheep/goats."
"723","“Glory be to him whose praise the thunderclap sings and the angels glorify in awe of him”. He used to say, then, that the thunder-clap is a stern warning for the dwellers of earth."
"724","Awsat bin Ismail has narrated that he heard Abu Bakr (ra) say after the death of the Prophet (ﷺ) “This is the very place where the Prophet (ﷺ), had stood in the first year of Hijrah”. Saying that, he began to weep and added, \Hold on to truth because that is piety and both these things will carry a man to paradise. And"
"725","“O Allah, I ask you for all of the blessing.” He asked the man whether he knew what all the blessing meant and he said that it meant admittance to paradise and safety from Hell. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by another man who was saying: “O Allah! I ask you for patience”. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him, \You have asked your lord for trial and difficulty over yourself. So"
"726","Abbas bin Abdul Mmuttalib (ra) said that he requested the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to teach him a supplication whereby he May request Allah for his needs. The Prophet (ﷺ) said,\0 Abbas"
"727","(O Allah, let us have the good of this world and the good of the hereafter and save us from the torment of the fire)."
"728","O Allah, grant us what is good in this world and what is good in the hereafter, and save us from the chastisement of the fire.\ Then the Prophet (ﷺ) made a supplication for him and Allah"
"729","(O Allah, I seek refuge in you from the distress of trial and then stops. When he makes this supplication he should also say (except a trial that produces elevation of ranks)"
"730","Abu Hurayrah (ra) has narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) sought refuge in Allah from the distress of trial, being overtaken by a tribulation, malicious rejoicing of enemies, and perversity of fate."
"731","Abu Naufal bin Abu Aqrab has narrated on the authority of his father that he asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about (voluntary) fasts. He said,\observe one fast every month.\"" He submitted"
"732","Jabir bin Abdullah (ra) said that they were with the Prophet (ﷺ)when a very stinking gush of wind blew over there. The Prophet (ﷺ) they asked his companions (ra) if they knew what that was. He added, \It is the (stinking) air of those people who backbite the believers.\"""""
"733","Jabir (ra) said that (once) a bad smelling wind blew in the times of the prophet Ig. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said,\ The hypocrites are backbiting the Muslims. That is why this wind blows\"""""
"734","It is reported by Qasim bin Abdur Rahman as-Shami that he heard Ibn Unm Abd say, \If a believer is backbitten before someone and he helps the believer (by refuting backbiting) then Allah will reward him well in this world and the next. And"
"735","It is reported by Jabir bin Abdullah (ra) that they had accompanied the messenger of Allah when they came to two graves. Both the inmate of the graves were being punished. He said,\ They are being punished not for committing a grave sin. But"
"736","It is reported by Qays that Amr bin al-Aas (ra) was going somewhere with his friends. They saw a dead mule whose belly had swollen up. Amr (ra)said,\ By Allah"
"737","It is reported by Abu Hurayrah (ra) that Maiz bin Maalik al-Aslami (ra) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) repeatedly (so that he may be given the prescribed punishment for the sin he had committed). When he came the fourth time, the Prophet (ﷺ) gave orders for Rajam and he was stoned to death. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and a few of his companions afterwards passed by him. One of the companions remarked,\ How many times this perished man came to the Prophet"
"738","Ubadah bin Walid said that he came out with his father Ubadah bin al-Samit and he was a young man at that time. They met an elderly \nShaikh who had a mantle over him and Maafi garments. His slave too had a mantle and Maafai. The narrator (Ubadah bin Walid) said,\ My uncle! In this way"
"739","Muhammad bin Ziyad said that he found that the predecessors (that is, the companions and their successors) lived together with their families. When a guest of one of them arrived and he found the cooking pot of another on the stove, he would take it serve his guest from it. When the owner of the cooking pot found it missing, he would enquire and the man who had taken it would tell him that he took it for his guest. There upon the owner would exclaim.\ May Allah bless it for you"
"740","A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said, ""What is to be done with this woman?"" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said, ""Who will take her in or provide for her?"" A man from the Ansar said, ""I will."" So the Prophet, peace be upon him, sent him to his wife and said, ""Treat the guest of the Messenger of Allah well."" The woman said, ""We have nothing but food for the children."" He said, ""Prepare her food, and arrange her bed, and put her children to sleep when they want to sleep, then prepare her food again, and arrange her bed again, and let her children sleep again, then prepare her food once more, and arrange her bed once more, and let her children sleep once more, then she will be content."" Then she prepared her food, arranged her bed, and put her children to sleep, and when they wanted to sleep again, she prepared her food again, arranged her bed again, and let her children sleep again, and when they wanted to sleep once more, she prepared her food once more, arranged her bed once more, and let her children sleep once more, then she was content. Then she lit the fire, and they ate, and they stayed for two nights, then they woke up in the morning and came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and he said, ""Allah has laughed, or has been amazed, at your actions, and Allah has said, 'And they will be given preference over their own selves, even if there is a small amount of good in them, and whoever is saved from his own self, then those are the successful ones.'"""
"741","Abu Shurayh at Adawi (ra) said that his ears heard eyes observed that The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was saying,\ he who believes in Allah and the last day should honour his neighbor. He who believes in Allah and the Last Day should take great care of the Jaizah his guest.\"" (Jaizah is a provision for a guest that is superior to one’s everyday meal.) The narrator asked"
"742","Abu Hurayrah (ra) has reported that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said,\Hospitality extends over three days and what is beyond that (more than three days) is Sadaqah."""
